From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] store, package: answer a game's add-on queries and mount its
 add-ons

XPackageMount, XPackageGetMountPath and XStoreQueryAssociatedProducts /
XStoreQueryProducts answered E_NOTIMPL, so a game that reads its DLC from a
mounted package, or lists its add-ons from the Store, saw none even with
them installed and licensed.

XPackageMountWithUiAsync/Result and XPackageMountLegacy (Package/Mount.h)
now mount packages already extracted on disk: the current game's own folder
(the one holding its MicrosoftGame.config), and an installed content
package of it or of a related game, found exactly as
XPackageEnumeratePackages(Content) finds it (XODUS_CONTENT_ROOTS, the game's
DLC folder). A content package is mounted only with the account's signed
Durable licence for it, the same request XStoreAcquireLicenseForPackage
sends (xstore_content_license in Store/PackageLicense.h): being on disk is
never a licence. The mount path is the package's folder; nothing is copied.
An unknown or unrelated identifier fails at once with
E_GAMEPACKAGE_NO_PACKAGE_IDENTIFIER, a missing licence with E_ACCESSDENIED.
XPackageGetMountPathSize/GetMountPath/CloseMountHandle work on the handles.

XStoreQueryAssociatedProducts (and ...ForStoreId for the current game)
answers for the game's related products (MicrosoftGame.config's
RelatedProducts plus the launcher's NEXUS_RELATED_PRODUCT_IDS), owned or
not; XStoreQueryProducts for the products asked. Both go through the
entitled-products path with a catalog request (<Catalog>, <Describe>): the
game and its related products are sent for the signed licence as before,
an owned product keeps every receipt check, and a product the account does
not own is described from the public display catalogue only, out of the
collection, its full SKUs (four at most) with no end date. A catalog never
feeds the game-licence observer and never yields a licence
(store_license_until). Products not related are never sent for a licence.

tests/Nexus/package-content.cpp covers the mounts (licensed, unlicensed,
related game's add-on, unrelated, unknown, malformed, handle lifetime, the
async form) and the DLL's mount without a licence;
tests/Nexus/package-legacy{,-32}-probe.c the own-package mount;
tests/Nexus/store-entitlements.cpp the catalog request, the public
description, catalog parsing and its ownership rules, the products and
associated queries' argument checks and bridge failures, and the mount's
licence. Required check counts rise to 363 (package-content) and 153
(package-legacy).

Playport's lines in this patch are offered under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-xbox-addons-runtime.md
Offered-upstream: no
